      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have similar system from KatVR, named KatVR Loco, but as standalone system. This system is more or less same as Walk. It's not full solution for FBT because its limited in moving around. It detect only on walking and rotation. Kat software can translate it in motion but VRChat has different way on locomotion: it uses joysticks to go around, because you need jump too.\nDue different worlds in VRChat, i don't think Walk locomotion system will help much there. \nAnd why spend 700 EUR for solution which is only locomotion and not even FBT? For same price, you have already FBT system with Vive trackers.\nUnless you have too much money in your bag, go ahead.\nBack to Kat Loco, this has very limited FBT system because it can track how legs moves but cannot track feet+legs angle and where feets are (missing location tracking), it can only track angle of hips and legs with 3 trackers.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
